"""Fixtures for the Go gateway's read backends (A-9 S5a), generated by driving the Python adapters (reads.py, airframe_api.py,
engine/pg.py PgArtifacts) over canned upstream answers: the requests each sent (method, target, Accept and Authorization),
and what it returned, raised or refused with. gateway/internal/backends/testdata/{reads,artifacts}.json are read by the Go
tests, which serve the same canned answers from an httptest server and require the same requests and the same result.

Called by tools/gen_gateway_registry.py (outputs()), whose --check fails when a committed file differs.

A case may carry "go": a different expectation for Go, with "why": the places Go is deliberately stricter than Python.
"""
from __future__ import annotations

